    "b-20-vision-a-scene-engine-that-make-2": {
      "id": "b-20-vision-a-scene-engine-that-make-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A scene-engine that makes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "composition",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " the primary authoring activity. Define assets once in a project workspace, drop them into a scene, edit their properties visually or programmatically, then build the result as a deployable web page or packaged desktop authoring app. The first concrete deliverable is the Codecaine title screen: a layer-rich scene that exercises every major asset path end-to-end."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-vision-divider-3": {
      "id": "b-20-vision-divider-3",
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {},
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-vision-unity-scene-as-the-menta-4": {
      "id": "b-20-vision-unity-scene-as-the-menta-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Unity Scene as the Mental Model"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-vision-a-scene-corresponds-5": {
      "id": "b-20-vision-a-scene-corresponds-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A "
        },
        {
          "insert": "scene",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " corresponds 1:1 to a page. Each scene is one full stage (1440×1080), and assets are placed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "into",
          "attributes": {
            "italic": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " the scene as typed layers. This mirrors Unity: a Scene is the actual stage of the game, and everything for that stage is placed into it as assets."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-vision-scenes-are-not-interacti-6": {
      "id": "b-20-vision-scenes-are-not-interacti-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Scenes are not interactive applications. They are landing pages and static websites that "
        },
        {
          "insert": "feel",
          "attributes": {
            "italic": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " like video-game UI screens: title screens, menus, selection screens. The focus is on visual richness and composition, not application logic."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-vision-similarly-to-the-unity-7": {
      "id": "b-20-vision-similarly-to-the-unity-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "\"Similarly to the Unity naming, where a Scene is an actual stage of the game, and then everything for that stage is put in as assets into that scene.\"",
          "attributes": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-vision-asset-and-module-types-8": {
